   "text": {
    "L1": "When animals skip-count, each landing is a multiple of their jump size.",
    "L2": "A multiple list continues forever because we can always add another jump.",
    "L3": "A frog jumps 6 at a time, and a grasshopper jumps 8 at a time.",
    "L4": "Their landing lists are 6, 12, 18, 24 and 8, 16, 24.",
    "L5": "The first number in both lists is 24, so they first meet at 24.",
    "L6": "It is not 6 times 8, which is 48; listing shows the earlier common multiple.",
    "L7": "Factors divide a number, while multiples are numbers the number goes into.",
    "L8": "Now choose the first place where the frog and grasshopper land together."
   },
